     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is double the maximum labeled metformin dose. The usual limit is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nWas one of these intended?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release. The \"1700\" may have been a slip for 850, which is half of 1700.\n- **500 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 1,500 mg/day.\n- **1000 mg twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Another dose.** If you really do want 1700 mg per dose, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy or the attending first.\n\nTell me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
